# AngularJS Client

## Module and routing

- Root module: `rotApp`. Feature modules extend it (e.g. `rotApp.auth`, `rotApp.admin`).
- Routes via ui-router `$stateProvider` in feature `*.js` files.
- HTML5 mode enabled — use ui-sref, not hash URLs.

## Component pattern

Newer features use ES6 classes registered as components:

```javascript
class MyComponent {
  constructor($http) { this.http = $http; }
  $onInit() { /* load data */ }
}
angular.module('rotApp').component('myComponent', {
  templateUrl: 'app/myFeature/myFeature.html',
  controller: MyComponent
});
```

## Templates and data

- Colocate `*.html`, `*.css`, `*.js` per feature under `client/app/<feature>/`.
- `$http` calls hit `/api/*` or file routes (`/fileserver`, `/pdf`).
- Auth check: `window.user && window.user.accessToken` (also Firebase login on main page).
- Use ui-grid for tabular data; Bootstrap classes for layout.

## Do not

- Introduce React, Vue, or Angular 2+ patterns.
- Add TypeScript or modern build tooling unless explicitly requested.
